# renderer-measurement
#
# Diagnostic, for the renderer and performance questions. Two things: (1) logs once which renderer SDL actually created and at what output size - that was guesswork before - and, when creation fails, captures SDL_GetError() immediately, before any fallback attempt, so the reported text is the failure's own; a file named 'renderer-driver' next to the binary names the driver to ask SDL for, a file and not an environment variable because the AROS Shell's setenv does not reach getenv(). (2) counts actual frame presentations in SoftwareDrawingEngine::present() over fixed 30-second windows, printing one [PRESENT] line per window (frames, fps, median, p90, max), so a window that falls entirely after the map is loaded describes gameplay rather than a mixture of startup, title screen and modal dialogs. NOT for upstream and not for a release build.
#
# Against OpenLoco 7f8c90cf (upstream-next), applied with -p1 by scripts/bootstrap.sh.
# Saved 2026-09-20, replacing the earlier version that timed main-loop iterations in Main.cpp. The five includes it still adds to Main.cpp are now unused; they are kept so this patch is exactly what build 833476c8... was made from.

